# Styling Rules

Prevent spaghetti styling. Prefer **shadcn component APIs** over ad-hoc Tailwind on every usage.

## Golden rule

**Style through props first. `className` is a last resort.**

Every shadcn primitive exposes intentional props — use them:

| Component | Prefer props |
|-----------|----------------|
| `Button` | `variant`, `size`, `asChild` |
| `Badge` | `variant` |
| `Alert` | `variant` |
| `Card` | compose `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardDescription`, `CardContent`, `CardFooter` |
| `Input` / `Label` | native props + minimal layout wrapper |
| `Tabs` / `Toggle` / `ToggleGroup` | component structure + variants |

```tsx
// ❌ Avoid
<Button className="bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white px-8 h-12 rounded-full">

// ✅ Prefer
<Button variant="default" size="lg">
```

## Where to change styles

| Change type | Location |
|-------------|----------|
| Brand-wide (accent, radius, colors) | `app/globals.css` CSS variables |
| All buttons / inputs / cards behave differently | `components/ui/<component>.tsx` |
| One-off layout (grid, flex, gap, max-width) | Consumer `className` on wrappers only |
| Lander section layout | `components/lander/<section>/` wrapper divs |

**If a UI pattern repeats across lander + app → update `components/ui/`, not each call site.**

## className usage (allowed vs discouraged)

### Allowed
- Layout containers: `flex`, `grid`, `gap-*`, `max-w-*`, `mx-auto`, `px-*`, `py-*`
- Responsive structure: `md:grid-cols-3`, `hidden md:flex`
- Typography: `.font-primary` for body/UI, `.font-secondary` for headlines — no tertiary font
- Spacing between sections: `space-y-*`, `mb-*`

### Discouraged
- Re-coloring primitives: `bg-*`, `text-*`, `border-*` on `Button`, `Badge`, `Input`, etc.
- Duplicated hover/focus/active styles on consumers
- Copy-pasting the same `className` string across multiple files
- Long chained utility strings (>5 utilities) on a single element — extract to `components/ui` variant or a small wrapper component

## Extending components correctly

When existing variants are not enough:

1. **Add a variant** in `components/ui/<component>.tsx` via `cva` — do not override in 10 places
2. **Compose** with existing subcomponents (`Card` + `CardHeader` + …)
3. **Create a lander-specific wrapper** only if layout is unique to marketing (e.g. `components/lander/pricing/pricing-card.tsx`) — still use `Card` + props inside, no raw div styled as a card

```tsx
// ✅ pricing-card.tsx — composition, not reinvention
<Card>
  <CardHeader>...</CardHeader>
  <CardContent>...</CardContent>
</Card>
```

## Theming

- Accent / primary / ring → `app/globals.css` (`--brand-accent`)
- Do not hardcode hex colors in components when a CSS variable or `variant` exists
- Dark mode via `.dark` class + shadcn tokens — not per-component dark: prefixes for colors

## Anti-patterns (spaghetti)

- Same button style copy-pasted in navbar, hero, pricing, footer
- `components/lander/` files that restyle shadcn internals with 15+ classes
- Inline `style={{ }}` for things Tailwind tokens handle
- Mixing one-off Framer Motion + custom CSS on every element

## Before finishing UI work

1. Grep for repeated `className` patterns — consolidate into `components/ui`
2. Confirm primitives use `variant` / `size` props
3. Confirm brand changes live in `globals.css` + `lib/constants/branding.ts`, not scattered hex values
